XmlParser:
Use when you need to update and read the XML simultaneously.
Ideal for scenarios where the entire XML document is processed or manipulated incrementally.
Example: Adding, removing, or modifying nodes directly.

XmlSlurper:
Use when you only need to read specific parts of an XML file.
Suitable for transforming an existing document into another format.
Example: Extracting values using GPath expressions without modifying the original XML.